+// What the viewer can see is a hold: the time between two consecutive
+// frames' reports, in vsyncs. A frame of duration d on a display of period p
+// is legitimately held floor(d/p) or ceil(d/p) vsyncs -- 2 or 3 for 24p on
+// 60 Hz, 5 or 6 for 23.976 on 120 Hz, exactly 1 for 24p on 24 Hz --
+// whichever of the two the platform picks and however its report clock is
+// offset. A longer hold lost the viewer a slot: that is a miss. The short
+// hold that immediately follows it is the same event catching up and is not
+// counted again; a short hold on its own is.
+struct present_hold {
+    bool valid;
+    uint64_t seq;        // the intent the report answered
+    int64_t system_nano; // the report
+    double duration_ns;  // the frame's display duration
+    int64_t period_ns;   // the grid the frame was timed on
+    bool long_hold;      // the hold that ended at this report was too long
